comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T21:27:34.572Z","harness:codex","GitHub intake: GH-1126 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1126. Reused the canonical annotation-facet grammar task. Red reproduction: comments/learnings reject --text even though notes/remind and collection concepts use text; human recovery can truncate before suggested_retry."
  "2026-08-26T21:34:26.811Z","harness:codex","TDD red: shared registration spec proves comments, notes, and learnings all reject the convergent --text alias before reaching their SDK adapters."
  "2026-08-26T22:51:39.094Z","harness:codex","Evidence for the implemented slice: comments, notes, and learnings now accept the convergent --text alias and reject conflicting positional/text payloads through one typed resolver; recovery bundles put suggested_retry first. Fresh-directory acceptance persisted and projected one entry from each collection. The linked sandbox-safe suite passed 134/134, while repository gates passed pnpm build, pnpm lint, 584 files and 8025 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, pnpm audit clean, and Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL vuln+secret+misconfig clean. This closes only the GitHub #1126 alias slice; the broader convergent grammar programme remains open for its other command families."
  "2026-08-27T02:27:12.211Z","harness:codex","Quality-gate evidence for PR 1128 review: pnpm build passed; pnpm lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, repository static quality, 100 percent docstring coverage, SDK/package parity, refusal closure, graph composition, and record integrity; node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage passed 584 files and 8031 tests with statements 59690/59690, branches 44928/44928, functions 12416/12416, and lines 57481/57481; pnpm security:scan found no credential-like tracked secrets; pnpm audit --audit-level high found no known vulnerabilities. pm-yql1 remains open because its broader programme scope is not complete."
  "2026-08-27T04:01:43.379Z","harness:codex","Review TDD red: CodeRabbit exact-head review 5037100816 reports the public --text contracts for comments, notes, and learnings are absent from generated Bash, Zsh, and Fish completion surfaces."
  "2026-08-27T04:07:19.515Z","harness:codex","TDD red (CodeRabbit exact-head follow-up): annotation completion regression fails because comments/notes/learnings command blocks omit the convergent public --text alias in Bash, Zsh, and Fish. Command: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/commands/completion-command.spec.ts."
  "2026-08-27T04:43:00.240Z","harness:codex","Review completion-slice evidence: generated Bash, Zsh, and Fish completion surfaces now expose the public --text alias for comments, notes, and learnings, with one shared Bash branch to avoid duplicated command blocks. Focused completion and surface-replication plans pass 122/122 with zero active semantic replication sets; linked annotation plans pass 134/134 plus completion 104/104. Full repository coverage remains exact 100/100/100/100. This completes the review-requested alias slice; the broader facet convergence programme remains unfinished."
  "2026-09-12T07:07:33.940Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: reuse the complete all-status inventory (2738 items; strict-read complete; no omissions) and existing alias/visibility lineage. Consolidate comments, notes, learnings, files, docs, deps, append and test under item using native handlers and public SDK operation identities. Preserve payloads, flags, SDK/MCP compatibility and literal text. Add parser, contract, shell and isolated-workspace acceptance proof."
  "2026-09-12T07:22:56.028Z","harness:codex","Continuation verification: complete strict-read inventory contains 2738 items with no omissions; current GitHub open PRs, issues, Dependabot alerts and code-scanning alerts are empty. Existing focused facet and internal-routing suite passes 16 tests in two files. Reclaim was refused because an existing claim is held; no override performed."
  "2026-09-12T07:27:20.444Z","harness:codex","Live graph evidence: all 2738 recorded nodes are connected with degree greater than one; 13653 edges, zero missing targets, and both ordering graphs acyclic. Semantic incidence is incomplete (1224/2738 overall; 201/311 active). Preserve meaningful chronology and use existing graph-governance lineage for historical enrichment; do not fabricate dependencies to achieve arbitrary depth. Ownership was renewed with ordinary release/claim, forced=false."
  "2026-09-12T07:29:00.755Z","harness:codex",Added real Bash execution coverage for item evidence flag suggestions and absence of internal worker/completion leaves. This extends acceptance beyond string snapshots; SDK/MCP operation names remain stable.
  "2026-09-12T07:39:50.675Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: full suite initially found 36 failures. Fixed nested files discover --id, semantic command suggestions, and canonical internal-worker census. Preserving the 4500-token contracts budget; installed package catalog currently exceeds the minimal projected receipt by 33 tokens and is being corrected without raising the budget."
  "2026-09-12T07:50:25.702Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: canonical facet addressing, semantic suggestions, error recovery, all shell completion generators, SDK action-scoped contracts, package helper registration, MCP graph family, grammar parity and release readiness tests passed in the focused batch. Default contract discovery now omits internal worker/completion plumbing at its source, preserving the existing 4500-token JSON budget; the earlier 33-token minimal-projection symptom did not require raising or changing budget enforcement. Full and explicitly scoped contracts retain internal paths. Generated contract and capability surfaces refreshed from SDK contracts."
  "2026-09-12T07:59:25.150Z","harness:codex","TDD completion finding: executing the generated Bash script for pm <TAB> failed to suggest item because the SDK capability census retained only item-reopen for the item entry. The census now retains both the actual item namespace and the compatibility operation, restoring root discoverability and Fish root-command detection. The same regression test exercises root and nested completion without mocks."
  "2026-09-12T08:02:02.647Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance passed again in a fresh temporary workspace: init/create/claim/start, all seven writable facets, seven canonical versus legacy read comparisons, linked command execution, structured close/release, and history plus resolution/drift validation. Packed npm/npx smoke, package-first dogfood and migration/read/write compatibility with published 2026.9.11 passed. Required Sentry/telemetry threshold gate passed with zero recent Sentry issues, 2.17 percent finish error rate and zero failures missing error codes. The broad suite exposed two remaining recovery expectation migrations and a duplicate list candidate after canonical alias projection; candidates are now deduplicated without changing their ranking."
  "2026-09-12T08:09:23.244Z","harness:codex","Tracker validation context: the 170 historical resolution warnings exactly match the deliberately unrecoverable residual enumerated in closed pm-e9zh (live status, resolution, notes and comments re-read). Its completed evidence recovery is not reopened or replaced with placeholder metadata. The concurrent corpus scan observed one hash mismatch on this actively updated item; direct history verification subsequently confirmed all 57 entries and the current document hash match. A frozen final corpus scan will follow closure. Local Greptile review of committed 17e2d7488 was unavailable because its free review quota is exhausted; this is not review approval."
  "2026-09-12T08:20:23.617Z","harness:codex","Final census found nested item files discover/lookup absent from destination and positional inventories. Red tests reproduced both; longest declared canonical-prefix operation resolution now preserves nested operation suffixes, and canonical census entries retain exact legacy positional slots. Added a no-growth 20-global-flag item budget and measured only its newly visible help baseline. Removed five phantom test-runs-worker flags from the historical inventory because executable worker registration never accepted them; no executable compatibility flag was removed. Focused descendant and full agent-task token regression suite now passes after settled rebuild; the earlier diagnostic mismatch does not reproduce."
  "2026-09-12T08:22:05.726Z","harness:codex","Manual semantic-contract review found canonical annotation --file flags classified as plan input rather than evidence-file input. Added canonical-versus-legacy concept assertions first, observed three failures, and resolved classification through stable operation identity. Corrected fixed compatibility census count from 3084 to 3079 after removing only the five non-executable worker declarations; seeded compatibility-removal and budget-growth controls remain mandatory."
  "2026-09-12T08:26:26.650Z","harness:codex","Final source review also inlined the one-use renderAttemptedCommand wrapper as required by repository quality guidance. The executable grammar census is now complete at 217 declared and 217 observed command paths, with 20 positional shapes within the unchanged budget of 21; no positional or destination findings remain."
  "2026-09-12T08:32:50.339Z","harness:codex","Correction to final-review notes: generic descendant-prefix resolution misclassified positional IDs during structured help. Replaced it with two explicit permanent SDK aliases for files discover/lookup, retaining exact-match semantics and automatic nested completion. The refusal census now includes both paths: 136 probes, 113 grammar contracts, 105 required-argument contracts. Also restored the command-rendering helper after the compiler identified its three call sites; it was not a single-use helper. These corrections supersede the earlier implementation notes."
  "2026-09-12T08:39:40.685Z","harness:codex","Continuation evidence: refreshed strict-read all-status corpus has 2738 items, complete with no omissions. Only this item, pm-lp4j and pm-szdc are in progress and under active delivery. GitHub open PRs and Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning alerts are empty; release incident GH-1239 recovered through the existing exact-tag job and canonical pm-7zs0. Full static and coverage gates are running on the current implementation."
  "2026-09-12T08:42:43.614Z","harness:codex","Live graph evidence: 2738 nodes, 13655 deduplicated directed edges, one connected component, zero missing targets, zero ordering cycles and complete typed outcome reachability. Seven preserved historical hierarchy conflicts remain informational, and 1512 nodes have no semantic edge under the graph classifier. Canonical facet acceptance now verifies the completed pm-zwpp SDK primitive lineage; no artificial dependency chains or duplicate items were introduced."
  "2026-09-12T08:44:46.608Z","harness:codex","Fresh continuation acceptance passed in a newly initialized temporary workspace: claim/start, seven writable facets, seven canonical/legacy read comparisons, linked node version test, structured close/release, history verification and resolution/history-drift validation. Packed npx and bunx smoke passed for 2026.9.12 across six package fixtures. Required reliability gate passed: zero Sentry issues in the 14-day window, telemetry finish error rate 2.17 percent and zero failures missing error codes. Backend recent-event query confirmed current command ingestion and the physical broker queue was empty."
  "2026-09-12T08:48:20.054Z","harness:codex","Continuation verification correction: concurrent broad verification and a linked-test rebuild overlapped writes to dist. Static subprocess output contains a transient module-export error and full coverage currently reports command-gate failures plus a timeout. These runs are not accepted as green evidence. Finish them, inspect exact failures, then serialize build-changing verification and rerun affected/full gates against settled output."
  "2026-09-12T09:07:46.060Z","harness:codex","Exact coverage evidence: all 8751 tests passed in 679 files after serialized verification. Coverage remains correctly red at 49004/49006 branches: the best-score replacement paths for canonical command suggestions lack namespace-specific assertions. Adding real Commander item-facet ranking cases to the existing facet contract suite, without mocks, threshold changes or production-code changes."
  "2026-09-12T09:09:12.376Z","harness:codex","TDD ranking finding: a real Commander fixture with item comments and commentary shows exact compatibility spelling comment ranked below the longer commentary prefix. The new namespace test fails on that ordering. Preserve SDK-declared exact aliases before fuzzy or semantic candidates, while requiring the canonical target to exist in the active runtime; typo and absent-target behavior remain covered."
  "2026-09-12T09:18:27.558Z","harness:codex","Final source verification: 679 files and all 8752 tests passed. Exact coverage is statements 64309/64309, branches 49010/49010, functions 13363/13363 and lines 61597/61597, with zero uncovered counts. Canonical exact-alias recovery now wins over longer fuzzy prefixes in an active Commander tree. Typecheck, focused lint, SDK compatibility, token budgets, isolated manual lifecycle, packed npx/bunx smoke, 88-command package-first dogfood, linked PM acceptance, dependency audit and tracked-secret scan passed. The earlier concurrent-build and uncovered-branch runs are superseded by this settled complete result."
